            <ArticleTitle>Horner's syndrome following tonsillectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>800-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tonsillectomy is one of the commonest procedures performed in the United Kingdom. Peri-operative infiltration of local anaesthetic is a well documented adjunct to post-operative analgesia. We report the first case of temporary Horner's syndrome in a patient who received such treatment and postulate an anatomical explanation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
